WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.940
Your storage lives in too many places.

2
00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:04.269
A few S3 buckets.

3
00:00:04.289 --> 00:00:05.877
A Google Cloud bucket.

4
00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:07.477
A folder on a server.

5
00:00:07.849 --> 00:00:10.179
Stowr shows all of them in one web page.

6
00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:14.619
One menu lists every bucket and every folder.

7
00:00:14.885 --> 00:00:18.475
Next to each name, you see what you can do there, and how full it is.

8
00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:22.198
Open a Markdown file, and you read it right there.

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.103
Open a CSV file, and it is a table.

10
00:00:25.123 --> 00:00:26.290
No download.

11
00:00:27.078 --> 00:00:28.906
Each bucket has its own page.

12
00:00:28.926 --> 00:00:31.888
Permissions, versioning, quota, free space.

13
00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.476
And the lifecycle rules?

14
00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:35.353
You edit them on the same page.

15
00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:40.134
It works with S3, MinIO, SeaweedFS and Garage.

16
00:00:40.335 --> 00:00:43.905
With Google Cloud Storage, and with plain server folders.

17
00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.786
One binary of 4.8 MB.

18
00:00:46.806 --> 00:00:49.305
One configuration file.

19
00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.080
One command to run it.

20
00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:52.244
Stowr.
